<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Hidden Hiqmah — Android 12+ splash mark.

  SOURCE OF TRUTH: apps/web/assets/splash-mark.svg, emitted by
  apps/web/scripts/gen-splash-mark.py. Edit the GENERATOR and re-derive; the
  generator asserts the geometry invariants (containment, clearances, minimum
  feature thickness) on every run, and hand-editing path data here silently
  discards those guarantees.

  WHY A VECTOR, NOT THE PNG BUCKETS IT REPLACES. The previous splash shipped as
  five rasters (288/432/576/864/1152) all derived from a ~512px master, so every
  bucket above mdpi was upscaled — which is what "grainy" actually was. It was
  never a sizing mistake: the buckets were dimensionally correct. A VectorDrawable
  is resolution-independent, so the problem cannot recur at any density, on any
  future screen, and it is one file instead of five.

  ⚠️ The density-bucket splash_icon.png files were DELETED when this landed. Do
  not reintroduce one: a drawable/ vector and a drawable-<dpi>/ raster of the same
  name are both valid candidates for the same resource, and which one wins is a
  density-resolution detail rather than a choice you get to make.

  GEOMETRY, measured rather than asserted (verified against the 1152px render):
    canvas        288dp
    ink diameter  176.0dp  — 8.0dp of headroom inside the 192dp circle that
                             Android 12 guarantees visible on a splash
    bbox          140.8 x 167.2dp (ratio 0.84)
  The old mark measured 198dp across — OUTSIDE the guaranteed circle, so its
  extremities were clipped — while being only 108dp wide, which is why it read as
  both small and cut off. The 176dp margin is ALREADY BAKED IN here: never run
  this art through gen-android-icons.py's furthest-ink safe-scale solve, or the
  margin gets applied a second time and the mark shrinks again.

  Two flat colours only, no gradients: #D4A843 is hiqmah_gold (the same value the
  notification channel and feature graphic use), #F8E8C8 the master's cream.
  Transparent by design — the black field comes from windowSplashScreenBackground
  in values/styles.xml, so this must never paint its own background.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="288dp"
    android:height="288dp"
    android:viewportWidth="288"
    android:viewportHeight="288">

    <!-- Mihrab arch: outer sweep down to the springline, walls to the book. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#D4A843"
        android:pathData="M 144 56 C 140 72 95 90 88 116 C 87.2 146 87.5 176 88.5 202 L 97.5 202 C 96.5 176 96.2 146 97 116 C 102.5 98 140.5 80 144 72 C 147.5 80 185.5 98 191 116 C 191.8 146 191.5 176 190.5 202 L 199.5 202 C 200.5 176 200.8 146 200 116 C 193 90 148 72 144 56 Z" />

    <!-- Eight-pointed star, solid and enlarged: the original's outline version
         fused into a blob below ~48px. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#D4A843"
        android:pathData="M 144 84.5 L 148.02 89.8 L 154.61 88.89 L 153.7 95.48 L 159 99.5 L 153.7 103.52 L 154.61 110.11 L 148.02 109.2 L 144 114.5 L 139.98 109.2 L 133.39 110.11 L 134.3 103.52 L 129 99.5 L 134.3 95.48 L 133.39 88.89 L 139.98 89.8 Z" />

    <!-- Open book: one solid form with a spine-gutter notch. The original's thin
         stacked page layers disappeared at small sizes. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#D4A843"
        android:pathData="M 144 208.5 L 138 199.5 C 118 201 88 196 73.55 189.75 A 84 84 0 0 0 85.65 204.42 C 100 214.5 124 220 144 223.5 C 164 220 188 214.5 202.35 204.42 A 84 84 0 0 0 214.45 189.75 C 200 196 170 201 150 199.5 Z" />

    <!-- Serif H. Counters kept open deliberately — they sealed into an "8" at
